{
  "_": "#NEW-79: the voice agent's tool policy, enforced by the LAUNCHER, never written into the model's prompt. Only the member's conversation session with the agent picked in Settings → Voice (`user_voice_settings.agent_id`; `sessions.brief` answers `voicePolicy: true` for exactly that root) runs under it: the claude CLI launches with `--permission-mode default` (never `--dangerously-skip-permissions`) plus flag settings that `ask` for Bash, Edit, Write, MultiEdit, NotebookEdit, WebFetch, Skill, Agent, Task and every MCP server of the launch (`mcp__exponential`, `mcp__codemode`, `mcp__computer` and each team server by its config name), so neither a user `allow` rule nor a PreToolUse allow skips `can_use_tool`, and that set `disableBypassPermissionsMode` (no subagent's `permissionMode` can bypass); a codex voice agent is refused at launch (codex has no `can_use_tool`); every other session keeps its bypass posture. Only the conversation's member answers its cards: `sessions.answer` / `sessions.resolveCard` refuse anyone else and an answer over the bus (`sessions.send {answer}`) is refused. `mcp__codemode__exec` is DENIED (a script reaches every op of every tool past the per-op tiers). ONE implementation replays this (apps/desktop/crates/domain/src/voice_policy.rs; the engine's claude adapter and the IDE's push to talk read it). CLASSIFY (`classifyCases`): `tier(tool, input)` = one of `tiers`. An Exponential tool (`mcp__exponential__exponential_<noun>`) reads `nouns[noun]`: `ops[input.op]` (an `ops` value is a tier, or `{tier, when: [{field, equals, tier}]}` whose first matching `when` wins), else the noun's `default`; a noun without ops (`sessions_send`, `guide_write`) is its `default`. A built-in tool reads `tools`; another MCP server's tool (`mcp__<server>__<tool>`) is `otherMcp` (outbound), except `tools` naming it; anything else is `unknown`. `AskUserQuestion` never meets the policy (it is the agent's own question card). TIERS: `auto` = allowed at once; `deny` = a plain deny (`permission_deny`, no interrupt) with `copy.denied`, so the model sees the error; `confirm` / `confirm-strong` = a proposal CARD: THE Dock ask the agent's own questions use (an elicitation: one step, options `options.allow` and `options.deny`, plus the folded free-text row; no new UI). CARD (`cardCases`): id = the tool call id (the idempotency key: answering twice is answering once). `header` = `copy.header` (confirm) or `copy.headerStrong` (confirm-strong). `question` = `{label} {target}` (the target only when there is one) + ` — {arguments}` when there are any + `.`, then for confirm-strong `copy.strongTail`, then, when the turn's person message is not blank, a blank line and `copy.snippet` with {text} = that message collapsed to one line and cut at `limits.snippet` characters (+ `…`). `label` = `nouns[noun].label` + ` · ` + the op in words (`_` → space), or `tools[tool].label` / `cards[tool].label`, else the tool name (`mcp__server__tool` → `server tool`). `target` = the first non-empty `targetKeys` value of the input (`cards[tool].target` for a built-in). `arguments` = every other input field except `op` in the call's order, blank, null and empty arrays skipped, `{key in words}: {value}` joined by `, `: a camelCase or snake_case key in lower words, a string value collapsed to one line and cut at `limits.value` characters (trailing spaces dropped, + `…`), quoted “…” when it holds a space, numbers and booleans as written, an array of scalars joined by `, `, an object `…`; at most `limits.arguments`, then `and {n} more`. REPLACE: a card's `replaceKey` = `{tool}|{target}` while its op is not a create (`createOps`) and it has a target, else null; a new card with the same key withdraws the older one (dismissed in the Dock, the older call denied with `copy.replaced`) (`replaceCases`). EXPIRY: an unanswered card is withdrawn after `expiresAfterMs` (denied with `copy.expired`). ANSWER (`answerCases`, `readAnswer(text)`): blank or `options.deny` = deny; `options.allow` = allow; else normalised as below: text that STARTS with a `no`, `deny` or `allDeny` phrase = deny; a `yes` or `allow` phrase and nothing else = allow; `[{yes}|{allow}] [,] {but} {change}` (a change word after an optional yes) = a change; anything else = other. Allow = allowed with the call's own input; deny (or the card dismissed) = denied with `copy.rejected`; other = denied with `copy.answered` ({answer} = the text), nothing pre-approved; a change on a card with an `approvalKey` = denied with `copy.changed` ({answer} = the text) and that key pre-approved for `preApprovedForMs`, ONCE, for a call of tier `confirm` or lower; a change on a card without an `approvalKey` = denied with `copy.changedAsk` and NOTHING pre-approved, so the redo asks again. `approvalKey` = `{tool}#{op}|{target}` (op = `input.op`, empty when absent) for a `confirm` card WITH a target, else null: a confirm-strong call or a call without a target is never pre-approved, and a redo with another op, another target, another tool or a higher tier asks again (`approvalCases`: the first call's card, the answer, the redo after `afterMs`, whether it runs without a card; `thenAgain` = whether a second identical redo would run too). SPEAKING: on the voice device Speak replies reads a waiting question card of the voice conversation aloud (`spokenText` of its question), which is the confirm-strong read-back. VOICE ANSWERS (`phraseCases`): `matchAnswer(text, cards)` runs on every finalized push-to-talk transcript BEFORE it goes out as a message; `cards` = `waitingCards(messages)` (`waitingCardCases`): the voice conversation's unanswered (`answeredAt` null) engine question cards (`card.kind` `question` with a `questionId`) whose `options` hold `options.allow` and `options.deny` and that are FRESH (createdAt parsed and `now - createdAt < expiresAfterMs`: a spoken yes never answers a card the engine already withdrew), oldest first (createdAt, then id), numbered from 1, each `{id, strong}` with strong = its question holds `copy.strongTail` (trimmed). Null = not an answer (the text is sent as a message); else the answers to post through `sessions.answer` {messageId: id, answer}. Normalise: lowercase, every character that is not a letter, digit, space or comma becomes a space, whitespace collapses (the `phrases` lists are normalised the same way, longest phrase first); a number is a digit, a `numbers` word or an `ordinals` word, optionally after `card` or `number`; `to` and `too` read as 2 right after an allow or deny word. Forms, first match wins, nothing else may follow: `{allAllow}` = every NON-strong card `options.allow` (null when every card is strong); `{allDeny}` = every card `options.deny`; `{allow} {n}` = card n `options.allow`, null when it is strong; `{yes} {n}` = card n `options.allow`; `[{allow}|{yes}] {n} [,] {but} {change}` = card n answered `Yes, but {change}`, null when it is strong unless it started with a `yes` word; `{deny} {n}` = card n `options.deny`; `{yes}` alone = the NEWEST card `options.allow`; `{yes} [,] {but} {change}` = the newest card `Yes, but {change}`; `{no}` alone = the newest card `options.deny`. A number past the last card, no cards, or anything else = null. {change} keeps the words as normalised.",
  "tiers": ["auto", "confirm", "confirm-strong", "deny"],
